# Large interactive 3D viewers (regenerate from scripts; too big for git).
#
# ⚠ This rule and CLAUDE.md's "every run writes its own figures beside its record, COMMITTED with the
# data" contradicted each other, and it was raised as PI decision 14 (2026-08-21) with a narrow
# exception proposed for the PHASE 1 render. The exception is NOT taken, because the conflict
# resolved a better way in the meantime: aleph/viz/cell_app.py renders the full cell natively and
# writes 1.5 MB PNGs instead of 78-124 MB pages. Those PNGs ARE committed, beside their record, so
# the charter is satisfied by the figures existing in a form worth committing rather than by an
# exemption for a format we stopped using. See aleph/outputs/ac/world_phase1/views/.
#
# The .alephcell binary stays ignored for the same reason as the HTML: it is 94 MB and it regenerates
# deterministically from world_export_cell.py given the same build, so it is DERIVED rather than
# evidence. The run record that IS evidence is committed.
aleph/outputs/mech_hier/figs/*_3d.html
aleph/outputs/mech_hier/figs/*_load_3d.html
aleph/outputs/mech_hier/figs/s3_nucleus_compression_3d.html
aleph/outputs/mech_hier/figs/s3_nucleus_incompressible_3d.html
aleph/outputs/**/*.html
aleph/outputs/**/*.alephcell

# polyscope viewer window-state (local UI state, never project state)
.polyscope.ini

# Outer-library built artifacts (decision A4 / stage 4 migration, 2026-08-09).
# They are outputs, and this tree's rule for outputs a pipeline can rebuild is the KB's rule: the
# source of truth is the thing that makes them, never the artifact. Provenance and rebuild
# instructions: aleph/outputs/outer/PROVENANCE.md
aleph/outputs/outer/**/*.npz
aleph/outputs/outer/**/*.jsonl
aleph/outputs/outer/**/*.jsonl.gz
aleph/outputs/outer/**/*.pt

# ── outer/ results are records, not build junk ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Line 18's bare `results/` was written for this tree's own scratch output and it silently ate 218
# files from the external-training corpus on 2026-08-09 — 174 manifest/receipt JSONs and, worse,
# seven trained `.pt` checkpoints. They were TRACKED in the source repository; a pattern written for
# one meaning of a directory name deleted them under another.
!aleph/outer/**/results/
!aleph/outer/**/results/**
aleph/outer/**/__pycache__/
aleph/outer/**/*.pyc

# ── the 14 built artifacts that live where the code writes them ───────────────────────────────
# Relocating these to `aleph/outputs/outer/` on 2026-08-09 was undone the same day: every module
# reads its own `results/` via `Path(__file__).parent`, so moving the payload out of the package
# did not make the pipeline read from two roots, it made it read a directory with holes. The
# coverage audit then reported 1,024 observation rows instead of 329,303 and 14 tests failed — an
# audit that counts absent files as a small number rather than refusing.
#
# So they sit where they are produced and are ignored here instead. **Listed by exact path, not by
# extension**: 26 `.jsonl` and 16 `.npz` under `aleph/outer/` are legitimately tracked evidence,
# and `model/combined_content/weights_title_only.npz` is tracked while
# `model/oa_content/weights_title_only.npz` is an artifact — same basename, opposite answer. Any
# glob wide enough to catch one silently untracks the other.
aleph/outer/acquisition/europe_pmc_oa_2026-08-05.jsonl
aleph/outer/acquisition/second_pass/candidates_2026-08-05.jsonl
aleph/outer/acquisition/second_pass/receipts_2026-08-05.jsonl
aleph/outer/experiment_factory/extraction/results/article_index.jsonl
aleph/outer/experiment_factory/extraction/results/figure_join_index.jsonl
aleph/outer/experiment_factory/learning/results/source_projection.jsonl
aleph/outer/experiment_factory/visual/results/asset_receipts.jsonl
aleph/outer/experiment_factory/visual/results/experiment_links.jsonl.gz
aleph/outer/experiment_factory/visual/results/visual_index.jsonl.gz
aleph/outer/model/combined_content/weights_combined_content.npz
aleph/outer/model/oa_content/weights_title_only.npz
aleph/outer/retrieval/combined/index.jsonl
aleph/outer/review_oa/results/article_screen_index.jsonl
aleph/outer/review_oa/second_pass/results/article_screen_index.jsonl

# C-1 setup-verification field dumps: mid-plane slices at full resolution, ~60 MB.
# The RENDER built from them is committed; the raw slices are reproducible from the driver.
aleph/outputs/ac/c1_*/verify_record.json
